  - "chest-x-ray"
  - "multi-label"
  - "audit"
abstract: >-
  A small, framework-agnostic Python library and CLI that audits a multi-label
  open-set recognition split for known-versus-unknown co-occurrence leakage.
  For every (unknown, known) label pair it computes the Miller-Madow
  bias-corrected mutual information in nats, with a paired bootstrap confidence
  interval and a permutation null on the worst pair, and returns a PASS/FAIL
  verdict against a leakage threshold (default 0.05 nats). A passing split
  bounds the harvestable co-occurrence signal before any model is trained, so a
  reported open-set ranking reflects detection rather than contamination.
